{"id":"1460222240973197318","date":"2021-11-15","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1460222240973197318","author":"markchen90","text":"@eriktorenberg While I agree with you on impact (I'm in tech now after all), many of my former colleagues would tell you that tech workers are delusional in how much they think their work changes the world. I think they're wrong 😉, but it's still a useful perspective to keep in mind.","reply_to":"markchen90","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20211115122500","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211115122500/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1460222240973197318","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1460222205313253376","date":"2021-11-15","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1460222205313253376","author":"markchen90","text":"@eriktorenberg Furthermore, since your contribution to firm PnL is often transparent, many firms will compensate you directly based on your contribution. I've noticed that in tech, how much you move the bottom line for the company is much less correlated with your take-home.","reply_to":"markchen90","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20211115122502","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211115122502/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1460222205313253376","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1460222170127208454","date":"2021-11-15","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1460222170127208454","author":"markchen90","text":"@eriktorenberg As someone who worked in trading for years before tech, it can take a lot of creativity to build a profitable trading strategy, and the financial reward for doing so can be as large as founding a unicorn.","reply_to":"eriktorenberg","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20211115122443","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211115122443/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1460222170127208454","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1436876274190880775","date":"2021-09-12","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1436876274190880775","author":"markchen90","text":"@twominutepapers I'd go as far as to say that having @twominutepapers or @ykilcher pick up one of my papers sometimes feels even more rewarding than getting it accepted at a conference. Do we need a Youtuber-index in Google scholar? (not serious)","reply_to":"markchen90","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20210912021703","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210912021703/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1436876274190880775","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
