{"id":"1373370119380824068","date":"2021-03-20","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1373370119380824068","author":"markchen90","text":"@ChrSzegedy @ericjang11 @drew_jaegle @BlackHC @pfau It's Table 4 here: https://t.co/tzIVg075Dp.\n\nOops, I misremembered just how strong the baseline was. 70% just from really good hparams entirely at 28x28 resolution.","reply_to":"ChrSzegedy","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20210320202542","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210320202542/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1373370119380824068","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1373358417310486531","date":"2021-03-20","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1373358417310486531","author":"markchen90","text":"@ChrSzegedy @ericjang11 @drew_jaegle @BlackHC @pfau Thanks! I actually wasn’t too bullish on this result since isometric nets got 70% working almost entirely at 32x32 (albeit with a jointly learned downsampler). Looking back in light of ViT, learned downsamplers are far more powerful than I imagined","reply_to":"ChrSzegedy","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20210320193911","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210320193911/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1373358417310486531","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1373353080167657472","date":"2021-03-20","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1373353080167657472","author":"markchen90","text":"@ChrSzegedy @ericjang11 @drew_jaegle @BlackHC @pfau Fully agree, I would love to see a strong result using only the supervised objective.","reply_to":"ChrSzegedy","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20210320191801","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210320191801/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1373353080167657472","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1373350098319466496","date":"2021-03-20","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1373350098319466496","author":"markchen90","text":"@ChrSzegedy @ericjang11 @drew_jaegle @BlackHC @pfau If we don't do the supervised fine-tuning, a linear classifier on self-supervised features gets ~95% and ~55% respectively.","reply_to":"markchen90","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20210320190610","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210320190610/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1373350098319466496","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1373349443601195013","date":"2021-03-20","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1373349443601195013","author":"markchen90","text":"@ChrSzegedy @ericjang11 @drew_jaegle @BlackHC @pfau We did self-supervised (BERT on pixels) training and then fine-tuned for the supervised task. Yes, the ImageNet result was on pixels, but first downsized to 32x32 resolution.","reply_to":"ChrSzegedy","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20210320190328","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210320190328/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1373349443601195013","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1373346076887973889","date":"2021-03-20","url":"https://x.com/markchen90/status/1373346076887973889","author":"markchen90","text":"@ChrSzegedy @ericjang11 @drew_jaegle @BlackHC @pfau We trained a permutation invariant model with learned position embeddings in Image GPT. At 32x32 resolution, we got 98.6% on CIFAR-10 and 66.5% on ImageNet.","reply_to":"ChrSzegedy","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20210320185010","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210320185010/https://twitter.com/markchen90/status/1373346076887973889","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
